From: hmhmdcy <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: samurai: enable the stock QUP1 I2C bus

The saved Android tree uses GPIO114/115 and QUP1 at 400kHz for the
MP2650. Enable the matching wrapper, DMA and controller for bounded
register observations. No charging client or policy is added.

Signed-off-by: hmhmdcy <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-samurai.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-samurai.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-samurai.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-samurai.dts
@@ -349,6 +349,20 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* Stock QUP1 wiring; no charger client or charging policy is bound. */
+&gpi_dma0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&qupv3_id_0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&i2c1 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 /* Stock BQ28Z610 at QUP15: standard read-only battery monitoring. */
 &i2c15 {
 	clock-frequency = <100000>;
